:ruby
  PageHeader = import("/components/PageHeader.haml")
  DocsPage = import("/components/DocsPage.haml")
  DocsSection = import("/components/DocsSection.haml")

%DocsPage
  %PageHeader{
    kicker: "Plugin Reference",
    title: "IntlPlugin",
    summary: "IntlPlugin parses Haml translation companions and lets Haml components receive locale-keyed translation data."
  }

  %DocsSection{ title: "Companion Files" }
    :markdown
      Intl files are companions to Haml modules.

      ```text
      components/Greeting.haml
      components/Greeting.intl.en.toml
      components/Greeting.intl.sv.toml
      ```

      `HamlPlugin` asks the build context for a plugin that responds to `translations_for`. If `IntlPlugin` is absent, Haml still compiles and receives an empty translation map.

  %DocsSection{ title: "Framework Responsibility" }
    :markdown
      Locale negotiation, missing-key behavior, interpolation, and helpers such as `I18n.t(:title)` are framework concerns. The example app handles that in `Example::I18n` and request-local context.

  %DocsSection{ title: "Development Reloading" }
    :markdown
      Adding, editing, or removing intl companions invalidates the owning Haml module, even when the companion file was not already in the dependency graph.
